{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q422434","formula":"KClO₄","hill":"ClKO4","elements":["O","Cl","K"],"composition":{"K":1.0,"O":4.0,"Cl":1.0},"names":{"en":"Potassium perchlorate","ru":"Перхлорат калия","uk":"Перхлорат калію"},"descriptions":{"en":"Potassium perchlorate is the inorganic salt with the chemical formula KClO4. Like other perchlorates, this salt is a strong oxidizer when the solid is heated at high temperature, although it usually reacts very slowly in solution with reducing agents or organic substances. This colorless crystalline solid is a common oxidizer used in fireworks, ammunition percussion caps, and explosive primers, and is used variously in propellants, flash compositions, stars, and sparklers.","ru":"Перхлора́т ка́лия, хлорноки́слый ка́лий — химическое соединение, калиевая соль хлорной кислоты с формулой KClO4, очень сильный окислитель.","uk":"Перхлора́т ка́лію, хлорноки́слий ка́лій — хімічна сполука, калієва сіль хлорної кислоти з формулою KClO4, дуже сильний окислювач."},"fame":45,"pubchemCid":24505,"mass":138.55,"charge":0,"smiles":"[O-]Cl(=O)(=O)=O.[K+]","inchikey":"YLMGFJXSLBMXHK-UHFFFAOYSA-M","iupac":"potassium perchlorate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-23526","atoms":24,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[8.751,0.0,0.0],[0.0,5.613,0.0],[0.0,0.0,7.198]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":5.957,"y":1.403,"z":1.155,"el":"K"},{"x":2.794,"y":4.21,"z":6.043,"el":"K"},{"x":7.169,"y":4.21,"z":4.754,"el":"K"},{"x":1.582,"y":1.403,"z":2.444,"el":"K"},{"x":4.984,"y":1.403,"z":4.953,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.767,"y":4.21,"z":2.244,"el":"Cl"},{"x":8.143,"y":4.21,"z":1.355,"el":"Cl"},{"x":0.608,"y":1.403,"z":5.843,"el":"Cl"},{"x":3.719,"y":1.403,"z":4.271,"el":"O"},{"x":5.032,"y":4.21,"z":2.927,"el":"O"},{"x":0.656,"y":4.21,"z":0.672,"el":"O"},{"x":8.094,"y":1